WEBVTT

00:04.000 --> 00:06.137
What's wrong with the TV.
Nothing, Chris.

00:06.182 --> 00:07.452
All the shows are
in widescreen now.

00:07.520 --> 00:09.375
So you can see all
the stuff on the sides

00:09.443 --> 00:10.946
that you
couldn't before.

00:11.014 --> 00:12.283
<i>ANNOUNCER:
We now return to The Brady Bunch.</i>

00:12.350 --> 00:13.286
See, look.

00:13.353 --> 00:14.756
Here's what you used to see.

00:14.824 --> 00:15.759
Good night, Mike.

00:15.827 --> 00:16.963
Good night, Carol.

00:17.031 --> 00:18.901
And here's the stuff you missed.

00:26.859 --> 00:30.735
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:30.803 --> 00:34.161
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:34.230 --> 00:37.287
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:37.371 --> 00:40.262
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:40.329 --> 00:44.224
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:44.291 --> 00:47.316
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:47.400 --> 00:48.936
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:49.004 --> 00:50.675
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:50.743 --> 00:52.512
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

01:02.843 --> 01:04.179
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

01:04.248 --> 01:05.550
Diane can't be with us today.

01:05.618 --> 01:06.686
Where is Diane, Ollie?

01:06.754 --> 01:08.224
She dead!
Thanks, Ollie.

01:08.292 --> 01:09.728
Yes, Diane is no longer with us.

01:09.795 --> 01:11.433
She was shot by
an unknown assailant,

01:11.501 --> 01:14.057
after she herself committed
a series of gruesome murders.

01:14.124 --> 01:16.497
I'd like to welcome
our new co-anchor, Joyce Kinney.

01:16.565 --> 01:18.102
Welcome, Joyce.
Thanks, Tom.

01:18.170 --> 01:20.643
Wow, you sound crazy nervous.

01:20.711 --> 01:22.514
In local news,
there was a hit-and-run

01:22.582 --> 01:24.586
by a drunk driver today
at Quahog Park.

01:24.655 --> 01:25.857
Two children are missing.

01:25.925 --> 01:26.894
(gasps)

01:26.961 --> 01:28.866
I was just there.

01:28.934 --> 01:30.153
Oh, boy.

01:30.220 --> 01:31.757
Don't let Brian see this.

01:31.825 --> 01:33.745
It says here that Rush Limbaugh

01:33.813 --> 01:35.568
will be signing books
at the Quahog Mall.

01:35.636 --> 01:37.173
BRIAN (in distance):
I have very good hearing!

01:37.240 --> 01:38.343
(footsteps approaching)

01:38.410 --> 01:39.479
He's awful.

01:39.547 --> 01:40.967
But I thought
Rush Limbaugh is

01:41.035 --> 01:43.322
a fictional character
played by Fred Savage.

01:43.391 --> 01:44.326
Where'd you
hear that?

01:44.394 --> 01:45.346
Fox News.

01:45.414 --> 01:46.448
Then it's a lie.

01:46.532 --> 01:48.037
Everything Fox News
says is a lie.

01:48.105 --> 01:49.374
But this one's true, Mom.

01:49.441 --> 01:51.078
You saw it with your own eyes

01:51.129 --> 01:53.084
and then you reported it
on Fox News.

01:53.152 --> 01:56.594
Even true things, once said
on Fox News, become lies.

01:56.663 --> 01:57.999
Why's Limbaugh
coming here?

01:58.066 --> 02:01.173
Don't they have bookstores
at the Nazi fascist...

02:01.241 --> 02:03.748
fascist fat camp
where he, where he go--

02:03.816 --> 02:05.318
where he, where he is
a counselor?

02:05.386 --> 02:06.791
I tell you what, Brian,

02:06.858 --> 02:08.728
if you want, we'll give you
another crack at that.

02:08.797 --> 02:11.302
This guy single-handedly
set political discourse back

02:11.353 --> 02:12.606
a hundred years.

02:12.674 --> 02:14.110
You know what? I'm
gonna go down there

02:14.178 --> 02:16.316
and give that bastard
Limbaugh a piece of my mind.

02:16.384 --> 02:19.292
But first I'm gonna sit here and
stare at this brown paper bag

02:19.359 --> 02:21.230
I'm pretty sure has food in it.

02:24.608 --> 02:25.576
(sniffing)

02:25.643 --> 02:26.545
PETER:
No!

02:26.613 --> 02:27.448
Ah, oh, well.

02:34.336 --> 02:35.555
Look at him.

02:35.639 --> 02:38.044
His side screwed up our country
for a generation.

02:38.112 --> 02:39.282
I hate everything
about that man.

02:39.350 --> 02:40.886
I'm gonna go
tear him a new one.

02:40.953 --> 02:42.993
I'm gonna go find some
hardcover photography books

02:43.060 --> 02:46.067
of tasteful nudes.

02:46.135 --> 02:49.009
Oh, my God, yes,
that is tasteful.

02:51.969 --> 02:54.056
Hey, my friend,
who should I make this out to?

02:54.124 --> 02:55.812
Listen, Limbaugh, my
name is Brian Griffin,

02:55.880 --> 02:57.750
and I have got
something to say to you.

02:57.818 --> 02:59.488
Our republic has
been bastardized

02:59.557 --> 03:01.594
and royally screwed up
thanks to you jackasses.

03:01.663 --> 03:02.631
You suck!

03:02.698 --> 03:03.868
And you're terrible.

03:03.936 --> 03:05.472
And... and-and
you've div--

03:05.540 --> 03:07.378
you've been divorced
several times.

03:07.445 --> 03:09.483
Yes, uh, valid points
you're raising, my friend,

03:09.552 --> 03:10.922
and I respect you
for raising them.

03:10.988 --> 03:12.442
But may I ask you a question?

03:12.510 --> 03:13.446
Okay.

03:13.512 --> 03:14.581
Have you ever read

03:14.649 --> 03:15.852
anything I've written?

03:15.920 --> 03:17.356
Well, no, I haven't.

03:17.423 --> 03:19.161
But I've read things
other people have written

03:19.229 --> 03:21.368
about the things you've written,
and I do not approve

03:21.435 --> 03:22.838
of the things
I've read from others

03:22.907 --> 03:24.242
about the things
they've read from you.

03:24.310 --> 03:25.446
Not one bit, sir.

03:25.481 --> 03:28.020
For crying out loud, Brian,
read my book.

03:28.087 --> 03:29.356
Judge for yourself.

03:29.424 --> 03:32.632
I'd sooner spend a night
watching European porn.

03:32.700 --> 03:34.772
<i>MAN (moaning):
Provo! Provo!
WOMAN (moaning):
Ah-shnork! Ah-shnork!</i>

03:34.839 --> 03:36.778
<i>Provo!
Ah-shnork!</i>

03:36.845 --> 03:39.217
<i>(loudly):
Provo! Provo!
(loudly):
Ah-shnork! Ah-shnork!</i>

03:39.285 --> 03:41.258
<i>Kaloooooof!
A'gerta!</i>

03:44.969 --> 03:47.207
Stupid right-wing dick.

03:47.274 --> 03:49.079
Yeah, you--
Hey, y-you want to sign my book?

03:49.131 --> 03:51.568
Yeah, you can sign my ass book.

03:51.637 --> 03:53.309
Is what would've been
awesome to say.

03:56.801 --> 04:00.611
Oh, no. It's a multiracial
TV gang, including white guys.

04:00.679 --> 04:03.135
Well, well,
what do we got here?

04:03.203 --> 04:05.476
Let's beat him up,
but not because of his color,

04:05.544 --> 04:07.582
'cause that doesn't
matter to us.

04:32.954 --> 04:34.424
(blows landing)

05:01.969 --> 05:02.972
Wow.

05:03.039 --> 05:04.242
Thanks, Rush.

05:04.309 --> 05:05.729
Ah, it was nothing.
I mean, you'd have

05:05.798 --> 05:06.698
done the same
thing for me.

05:06.766 --> 05:08.688
Uh, yeah, of course.

05:08.756 --> 05:10.726
Hey, you-you
dropped something.

05:10.794 --> 05:12.698
You think you might
give it a read now?

05:12.766 --> 05:14.804
Uh, well...

05:14.872 --> 05:16.995
What-What if I stick a piece
of bologna in the book,

05:17.063 --> 05:18.433
and I don't tell you which page?

05:18.499 --> 05:19.902
Would you read it, then, Brian?

05:19.971 --> 05:21.991
Would you read it to find
the page with the bologna?

05:22.060 --> 05:24.533
Okay, look, I'll read
four pages of your book tonight.

05:24.601 --> 05:25.602
All right?
Four pages.

05:25.670 --> 05:26.673
That's it.

05:26.740 --> 05:28.410
And maybe more
if tonight's episode

05:28.477 --> 05:29.881
<i>of The Office
ends up sucking.</i>

05:32.388 --> 05:34.025
(sighs)

05:34.094 --> 05:35.029
Four pages. Done.

05:35.097 --> 05:36.717
Moving on.

05:36.785 --> 05:39.842
RAINN WILSON:
I know my staplers
by sound and by weight.

05:39.911 --> 05:42.835
And that stapler, good sir,
is a "Schrute."

05:42.903 --> 05:46.043
Ha! Look at John Krasinski
look at the camera.

05:46.110 --> 05:47.598
He can't believe
this guy!

05:47.665 --> 05:49.068
(remote clicks)

05:49.136 --> 05:51.593
Aw, but there were gonna be
more high jinks in Scranton.

05:51.661 --> 05:53.581
(giggles):
Scranton.

05:53.650 --> 05:54.802
Dunder Mifflin.

05:54.869 --> 05:55.905
(giggles)

05:55.971 --> 05:58.294
Funny words
are funny.

06:15.110 --> 06:16.730
Oh, my God.

06:16.797 --> 06:18.803
Rush Limbaugh
was right all along.

06:18.871 --> 06:21.811
Conservative Republicanism
is the answer.

06:21.879 --> 06:23.750
Good. Good for Brian.

06:23.818 --> 06:24.904
Brian, look at this.

06:24.972 --> 06:26.792
Now, this is a
tasteful nude.

06:26.859 --> 06:30.302
It's called "A Saucy Outing
In Tottenham Court Square."

06:36.387 --> 06:38.993
Brian, are you reading the
new Rush Limbaugh book?

06:39.062 --> 06:40.999
Yeah, I picked it up
at the mall yesterday.

06:41.067 --> 06:42.470
I-I can't believe
I'm saying this,

06:42.538 --> 06:45.429
but this might be
the best book I've ever read.

06:45.497 --> 06:46.599
Brian, you got
to be joking.

06:46.667 --> 06:48.136
No, I mean it, Lois.

06:48.203 --> 06:50.542
You know, I've never actually
read any of Limbaugh's stuff,

06:50.610 --> 06:52.482
but this book
makes an excellent case for

06:52.550 --> 06:54.771
personal accountability,
fiscal responsibility

06:54.839 --> 06:56.008
and steak eatership.

06:56.075 --> 06:58.283
But you're a
hard-core liberal.

06:58.334 --> 07:00.605
Rush Limbaugh is a
right-wing extremist.

07:00.672 --> 07:02.844
He stands for
everything you despise.

07:02.912 --> 07:04.683
My loyalty is to reason, Lois.

07:04.751 --> 07:07.056
And as a reasonable person,
I reserve the right

07:07.124 --> 07:08.678
to change my mind
when presented with

07:08.745 --> 07:10.684
new information
that alters my perspective.

07:10.752 --> 07:13.107
And I got to tell you,
I had this guy all wrong.

07:13.191 --> 07:16.199
I mean, some of the stuff
in here is-- hey, bologna!

07:20.378 --> 07:21.731
Thank you, friends.

07:21.799 --> 07:24.254
It's always a pleasure
to meet regular, real Americans.

07:24.322 --> 07:25.107
Love the
Hummer, Rush.

07:25.175 --> 07:26.178
How do you like it?

07:26.262 --> 07:27.714
It is the best.

07:27.783 --> 07:30.205
I'm not saying you'd have to be
gay to drive something else.

07:30.273 --> 07:31.727
But if you drive
something else,

07:31.794 --> 07:34.350
you're probably a guy who likes
to pleasure other men sexually.

07:34.418 --> 07:35.454
(murmurs of agreement)

07:35.504 --> 07:37.258
Hey, it's my new
friend, Brian!

07:37.325 --> 07:38.262
Hi, Rush.

07:38.330 --> 07:40.133
Listen, I-I have to tell you,

07:40.184 --> 07:42.557
I read your book
and it was very persuasive.

07:42.624 --> 07:43.894
I knew you'd like it,

07:43.962 --> 07:45.699
and I'm glad you enjoyed
it, Brian, I really am.

07:45.767 --> 07:47.405
Oh, I-I more than enjoyed it.

07:47.473 --> 07:49.677
Ev-Every page
just spoke to

07:49.745 --> 07:51.683
And-And, you know,
talking to you now, I just,

07:51.751 --> 07:53.170
I-I want to find
the right words

07:53.238 --> 07:54.942
to describe how much
I agree with you.

07:55.010 --> 07:56.346
I got the
words, Brian.

07:56.414 --> 07:58.351
"Thank you, Rush,
for doing my thinking for me,

07:58.419 --> 08:00.089
"'cause I lack
the ability to think

08:00.157 --> 08:01.962
critically and independently."
Yes, that!

08:02.030 --> 08:03.566
You should be proud
of yourself, Brian.

08:03.634 --> 08:05.305
I mean, you sound like
a thoughtful American.

08:05.372 --> 08:07.762
Well, listen, I'd really love
to pick your brain some more

08:07.830 --> 08:09.231
and hear some of
your other thoughts

08:09.299 --> 08:10.703
about what's going on
in this country.

08:10.771 --> 08:13.278
I can do even better
than that, Brian.

08:25.078 --> 08:26.214
Wow.

08:26.281 --> 08:27.483
Never thought
I'd set foot

08:27.551 --> 08:29.223
inside Republican
National Headquarters.

08:29.290 --> 08:30.325
This is amazing.

08:30.392 --> 08:31.762
And it gets better, Brian.

08:31.830 --> 08:34.269
Come on, I'm gonna introduce you
to some of my pals here.

08:34.353 --> 08:36.475
Brian, meet George W. Bush.

08:36.544 --> 08:37.579
Hey, Georgie!

08:37.647 --> 08:39.835
Uncle Rush!

08:39.903 --> 08:41.725
(chuckles):
Hey! Whoo!

08:41.792 --> 08:43.161
You are getting heavy.

08:43.229 --> 08:45.501
I know.
I'm 64 and three-quarters.

08:45.569 --> 08:47.039
You sure are, slugger.

08:47.107 --> 08:48.810
Hey, you got one for me?

08:48.878 --> 08:50.098
What? What are you
talking about?

08:50.166 --> 08:51.936
Oh, come on, Uncle Rush.

08:52.004 --> 08:53.240
I-I don't know what
you're talking about, really.

08:53.308 --> 08:54.611
Come on!

08:54.678 --> 08:58.287
Oh. Wait a second.

08:58.339 --> 08:59.541
Yay! Yippee!

08:59.609 --> 09:00.643
Thanks, Uncle Rush!

09:00.712 --> 09:02.065
Don't tell my dad.

09:02.133 --> 09:04.070
Hey, there, Rush.
How you doing?

09:04.138 --> 09:05.274
Hey, John.

09:05.342 --> 09:06.979
Hey, I'd like you to meet
my friend, Brian.

09:07.047 --> 09:08.651
Brian, John McCain.

09:08.718 --> 09:10.389
Gosh, it sure is
a pleasure, Mr. McCain.

09:10.456 --> 09:12.077
How do you two know each other?

09:12.144 --> 09:14.149
Oh, Rush and I used to
solve mysteries together

09:14.217 --> 09:15.186
back in the day.

09:18.731 --> 09:20.517
I don't understand, John.

09:20.584 --> 09:23.593
The groundskeeper said he saw
the mummy burning the flag.

09:23.661 --> 09:25.431
But mummies don't
hate America.

09:25.498 --> 09:26.635
They sure
don't, Rush.

09:26.703 --> 09:28.206
But Democrats do.

09:28.274 --> 09:29.576
Ruh-roh.

09:29.644 --> 09:30.880
Remocrats.

09:30.948 --> 09:32.234
(teeth rattling)

09:32.319 --> 09:33.872
Oh, it's okay, Hot Dog.

09:33.939 --> 09:37.548
But I think it's time we unravel
the mummy and the mystery.

09:41.193 --> 09:42.596
I don't get
it, John.

09:42.664 --> 09:44.837
How's a pig gonna help
us lure the mummy?

09:44.905 --> 09:48.180
Rush, I've never known
a Democrat to pass up pork.

09:48.247 --> 09:50.050
(snickering)

09:51.255 --> 09:53.644
(moaning)

09:55.634 --> 09:56.971
Gotcha!

09:58.124 --> 09:59.812
Now let's find out

09:59.880 --> 10:02.602
who you really are.

10:02.653 --> 10:04.441
RUSH and JOHN:
It's old man Barney Frank!

10:04.509 --> 10:06.380
And I would have
gotten away with it, too,

10:06.447 --> 10:08.754
if it weren't for you
meddling Republicans.

10:08.822 --> 10:10.492
Thanks for all your help,
Globetrotters.

10:10.559 --> 10:12.565
That was a cold swish.

10:12.632 --> 10:13.801
Put her there.

10:13.869 --> 10:15.539
Aw, no, no, no, no.

10:15.607 --> 10:18.582
(laughter)

10:21.040 --> 10:24.314
Look, Brian, all I'm saying is,
it's not normal for people

10:24.383 --> 10:27.272
to change their political views
so radically overnight.

10:27.341 --> 10:29.579
Lois, no offense,
but you don't exactly know

10:29.647 --> 10:30.999
what you're talking about.

10:31.068 --> 10:32.337
I mean, you're-you're not
exactly a fountain

10:32.405 --> 10:34.009
of political knowledge yourself.

10:34.077 --> 10:36.549
(sighs) You want to know
what I think is happening here?

10:36.617 --> 10:38.421
Oh, this should be
rich and overtaxed.

10:38.488 --> 10:40.861
I think you just got to be
in the "out" group.

10:40.928 --> 10:43.753
Whoever's on top, whoever's
in power, whoever's successful,

10:43.820 --> 10:45.759
you got to be
on the other side

10:45.826 --> 10:48.064
or you don't feel like
the smartest guy in the room.

10:48.133 --> 10:50.238
All you are, my dear,
is a contrarian.

10:50.306 --> 10:52.477
Oh, please, you could
not be more off base.

10:52.545 --> 10:55.052
<i>Oh, yeah? Let me ask, what did
you think of the movie Titanic?</i>

10:55.119 --> 10:56.890
Horrible. One of the
worst movies ever made.

10:56.958 --> 10:58.662
<i>Mm-hmm. How about
Slumdog Millionaire?</i>

10:58.730 --> 11:00.098
Overrated. Just
a terrible movie.

11:00.166 --> 11:01.169
<i>Cocktail.</i>

11:01.236 --> 11:02.907
Actually, not
a bad film.

11:02.975 --> 11:04.896
You know, as classically
structured cinema,

11:04.964 --> 11:06.869
<i>Cocktail was one of the
best films of its era.</i>

11:06.936 --> 11:08.689
You make me sick, Brian.

11:08.757 --> 11:11.131
Look, Lois, if I were you,
I'd stow that attitude,

11:11.199 --> 11:13.470
because Rush Limbaugh is
coming over for dinner tonight.

11:17.683 --> 11:20.190
Lois, this dinner
looks delicious.

11:20.258 --> 11:21.426
Oh, well, thank you.

11:21.494 --> 11:22.529
Dig in, everyone.

11:22.597 --> 11:23.866
Whoa, hang on, hang on.

11:23.934 --> 11:25.337
I think you're forgetting
the grace, Lois.

11:25.405 --> 11:26.607
(sighs)

11:26.674 --> 11:30.351
Dear God who definitely
exists, we, your people,

11:30.419 --> 11:32.892
who have been on this
planet for 6,000 years

11:32.959 --> 11:35.833
and not a second more, wish
to thank you for this bounty,

11:35.901 --> 11:37.822
and for keeping Congress
predominantly white

11:37.890 --> 11:39.226
through Christ
our Lord, amen.

11:39.293 --> 11:42.703
So, Rush, I see you
made it here okay,

11:42.771 --> 11:45.978
driving on roads built with
public funds, by the government.

11:46.046 --> 11:47.583
Yeah, what about
that, Rush?

11:47.651 --> 11:49.706
I guess the government's
pretty good, like Lois says.

11:49.775 --> 11:52.397
Actually, I took the toll roads.
Privately built.

11:52.465 --> 11:54.987
Way smoother than the
crumbling public road system.

11:55.055 --> 11:57.143
Yeah, Lois. Government sucks
at doing stuff.

11:57.211 --> 11:58.982
Oh, no, toll roads
sound great.

11:59.050 --> 12:01.623
Too bad only the very rich
can afford to use them.

12:01.691 --> 12:02.793
I agree with Lois.

12:02.861 --> 12:04.364
Well, maybe more
people could

12:04.432 --> 12:06.636
if the government wasn't taxing
the bajeezus out of them.

12:06.704 --> 12:08.275
Now I agree with Rush.

12:08.343 --> 12:10.515
I'm too a'stupid
to make up my own mind.

12:10.584 --> 12:12.821
Yeah, okay. Whatever
you say, Rush.

12:12.889 --> 12:14.895
So... . nice
weather today.

12:14.962 --> 12:16.397
Yeah,
unseasonably cool.

12:16.466 --> 12:18.872
I guess we can forget
that whole global
warming myth.

12:18.940 --> 12:21.613
Global warming is not a myth,
you son of a bitch!

12:21.680 --> 12:23.334
Look, what the hell
are you so hostile for?

12:23.402 --> 12:25.373
Because you brainwashed
our dog.

12:25.441 --> 12:26.845
Hey, listen,
sister, I just...

12:26.913 --> 12:29.519
(farting)

12:29.587 --> 12:31.357
I'm sorry.

12:31.426 --> 12:34.867
Look, all I did was expose Brian
to a different way of thinking.

12:34.935 --> 12:37.073
He embraced... Oh, God,
I'm gonna move over here.

12:37.140 --> 12:38.913
He embraced it
on his own, Lois.

12:38.981 --> 12:40.482
Well, after Rush
opened my eyes,

12:40.550 --> 12:43.324
I am seeing the world
in a whole new way now.

12:43.392 --> 12:46.099
To quote a famous troublemaker,
"I have a dream..."

12:50.094 --> 12:53.620
♪ I dream of Republicantown ♪

12:53.671 --> 12:55.726
♪ Where men to the
right of the aisle ♪

12:55.794 --> 12:57.264
♪ Don't back down ♪

12:57.332 --> 13:01.074
♪ The streets are aglow
with the smell of apple pies ♪

13:01.142 --> 13:04.534
♪ And babies come out of the
womb in coats and ties... ♪

13:04.602 --> 13:05.904
Nice place, huh, Rush?

13:05.973 --> 13:07.710
It's a paradise, Brian.

13:07.795 --> 13:11.203
♪ Trees grow
from Republican sod ♪

13:11.271 --> 13:14.629
♪ And everyone prays to
a proper right-wing god ♪

13:14.697 --> 13:16.702
♪ Republican Catholics? ♪

13:16.770 --> 13:18.440
♪ Yes, indeed, there are ♪

13:18.509 --> 13:20.078
♪ Republican Muslims? ♪

13:20.147 --> 13:21.850
♪ Well, let's not
go too far ♪

13:21.918 --> 13:23.054
No Muslims?

13:23.121 --> 13:24.391
Nah, too many
tall buildings.

13:24.459 --> 13:27.181
♪ They've outlawed
all abortions ♪

13:27.250 --> 13:29.020
♪ Late or early ♪

13:29.088 --> 13:32.028
♪ It's a sin we can't abide ♪

13:32.096 --> 13:36.642
♪ What if you find
a fetus left abandoned? ♪

13:36.710 --> 13:39.483
♪ We just take it and
we jam it back inside ♪

13:39.551 --> 13:43.528
♪ Oh, yes, 'cause I dream
of Republicantown ♪

13:43.595 --> 13:47.272
♪ The place where the happiest
smile is Cheney's frown ♪

13:47.339 --> 13:50.815
♪ I'll bet you a buck y won't
find a damn thing wrong ♪

13:50.882 --> 13:52.804
♪ 'Cause when
you come down to it ♪

13:52.872 --> 13:55.828
♪ This is where we all belong ♪

13:55.880 --> 13:56.983
Who else lives here?

13:57.050 --> 13:58.571
Oh, big names, Lois.

13:58.638 --> 14:01.695
♪ We're watching
Republican stars ♪

14:01.763 --> 14:05.439
♪ Like sweet Mickey Rourke and
his gorgeous right-wing scars ♪

14:05.507 --> 14:07.462
♪ Chuck Norris is one ♪

14:07.530 --> 14:09.117
♪ And he's got
a right-wing beard ♪

14:09.185 --> 14:11.056
♪ Jon Voight is another ♪

14:11.140 --> 14:12.961
♪ He's just
right-wing weird... ♪

14:13.030 --> 14:15.885
His, uh... his daughter's
pretty hot, though.

14:15.938 --> 14:17.658
At one time, Brian.
At one time.

14:19.113 --> 14:21.702
♪ But how about
global warming? ♪

14:21.771 --> 14:23.943
♪ It's a snow job ♪

14:24.011 --> 14:26.600
♪ By Obama and his crew ♪

14:26.667 --> 14:31.030
♪ But aren't all his
findings backed by science? ♪

14:31.097 --> 14:33.553
♪ Careful, Lois, now
you're sounding like a Jew ♪

14:33.621 --> 14:34.673
Oy.

14:34.741 --> 14:38.149
♪ We dream of Republicantown ♪

14:38.216 --> 14:41.759
♪ Where Clinton is viewed
as a crazy commie clown ♪

14:41.827 --> 14:45.469
♪ A place where America's
growing free and strong ♪

14:45.538 --> 14:48.596
♪ 'Cause when you come down
to it, this is where ♪

14:48.664 --> 14:54.645
♪ We. all... belong. ♪

14:56.535 --> 14:59.276
Well, I got to tell you, I'm
not buying any of this crap.

14:59.343 --> 15:01.548
Rush, we want our dog back.

15:01.616 --> 15:02.985
Whoa, hang on, Lois.

15:03.054 --> 15:04.992
What are you saying?
I don't have a mind of my own?

15:05.060 --> 15:06.629
That's insulting.
And-and you know what?

15:06.680 --> 15:07.933
I don't, I don't
like the way

15:08.002 --> 15:09.621
you've been talking
to Rush this evening.

15:09.690 --> 15:11.493
You know, I-I thought
you were my friends.

15:11.577 --> 15:13.868
But if you can't accept me
now that we disagree

15:13.936 --> 15:15.672
about certain things, then
maybe you aren't the friends

15:15.740 --> 15:17.461
I thought you were.
I'm moving out.

15:17.529 --> 15:19.266
What?!
No!
Again?

15:19.333 --> 15:20.769
I'm gonna go stay
with Rush Limbaugh.

15:20.837 --> 15:22.275
Right, Rush?
Huh?

15:22.342 --> 15:23.611
I'm gonna
stay with you.

15:23.678 --> 15:25.316
Uh... yeah, yeah, sure.

15:25.384 --> 15:26.520
That-That's fine.

15:26.587 --> 15:29.060
Oh, this is a bad idea.

15:29.128 --> 15:31.299
But I guess sometimes
Fox has bad ideas, huh?

15:32.771 --> 15:34.794
Let's all just sit here
for a moment

15:34.861 --> 15:37.116
and remember that
this was a thing.

15:44.631 --> 15:45.500
Morning, Rush.

15:45.557 --> 15:47.262
Hey, thanks again
for letting me stay here.

15:47.330 --> 15:49.166
Oh, it's not really
any trouble, Brian.

15:49.234 --> 15:51.005
What do you figure,
just a few days?

15:51.073 --> 15:52.275
Aw, man, who knows?

15:52.343 --> 15:54.113
It's just so good
to be out of  there.

15:54.181 --> 15:55.952
Hey, you know, I've been
reading all your books

15:56.020 --> 15:58.042
and I so 100% agree with you.

15:58.109 --> 15:59.863
I mean, what is going
on with this country?

15:59.931 --> 16:01.534
I mean, wake up, America.

16:01.585 --> 16:04.576
I mean, these taxes, right?
I mean, am I right?

16:04.644 --> 16:05.847
About the taxes?
You know?

16:05.915 --> 16:07.016
Yeah, taxes are pretty high.

16:07.084 --> 16:08.822
Is-is-is that
a new coffee machine?

16:08.890 --> 16:11.129
Oh, yeah, I took the liberty
of replacing your old one

16:11.196 --> 16:12.548
with a new,
American-made coffee machine.

16:12.616 --> 16:14.672
(electrical crackling)

16:14.740 --> 16:16.410
In fact, I got
you a bunch

16:16.462 --> 16:17.964
of new, topnotch,
American-made stuff.

16:19.671 --> 16:21.273
What else did you buy?

16:21.359 --> 16:23.798
Oh, a couple things:
that light fixture...

16:23.866 --> 16:26.070
new heat regulator
on your stove...

16:26.122 --> 16:28.043
your man-bra...

16:28.111 --> 16:29.580
your garbage disposal...

16:29.649 --> 16:30.968
your dishwasher...

16:31.035 --> 16:32.104
and your new cat.

16:32.173 --> 16:34.762
(cow bellowing):
Moo.

16:39.175 --> 16:41.448
<i>And you're listening to
the Rush Limbaugh Show.</i>

16:41.515 --> 16:43.637
I want to take a moment
to give a shout-out

16:43.704 --> 16:46.746
to my good friend Ken Lay,
faked his own death,

16:46.814 --> 16:48.652
listening in on
a ham radio somewhere

16:48.719 --> 16:49.937
in international waters.

16:50.005 --> 16:51.242
Smooth sailin', Kenny Boy.

16:51.310 --> 16:52.930
Hey, Rush?

16:52.998 --> 16:54.601
Is it okay to
hang out in here?

16:54.670 --> 16:56.524
Wh... All right, fine, just
don't say anything, okay?

16:58.413 --> 17:01.086
So, friends, we were
talking about Nancy Pelosi.

17:01.154 --> 17:02.290
How do we stop her?

17:02.357 --> 17:03.760
How do we stop
the Pelosi agenda--

17:03.829 --> 17:05.215
Hey, I'll tell you how.

17:05.283 --> 17:07.621
You strap her to a board,
put a cloth in her mouth

17:07.689 --> 17:09.159
and pour water over it
to simulate drowning.

17:09.228 --> 17:10.447
Yeah! Small government!

17:10.514 --> 17:13.054
And why don't we take
a short break here, folks.

17:13.121 --> 17:14.156
We'll be right back.

17:14.225 --> 17:15.544
Brian, are you nuts?

17:15.595 --> 17:17.734
What the hell kind of show
you think I'm doing here?.

17:17.801 --> 17:19.755
Wha-What? What are you...
Come on. Pelosi's a monster.

17:19.823 --> 17:22.263
And she's addicted to crack.
Come on, you're with me on this.

17:22.331 --> 17:23.666
Of course she's
addicted to crack,

17:23.734 --> 17:25.105
but you can't just say that.

17:25.173 --> 17:27.510
You got to lead people there
with an intelligent argument

17:27.579 --> 17:29.516
so they arrive at it
on their own.

17:29.584 --> 17:31.372
Hey, come on, man. We got to
tell people how it is.

17:31.440 --> 17:32.759
We got to get them
on board with us.

17:32.827 --> 17:35.333
Brian, look, there is no
victory unless people know why

17:35.401 --> 17:37.873
they were wrong to disagree
with you in the first place.

17:37.942 --> 17:39.680
Boy, do you sound soft.

17:39.748 --> 17:41.116
What the hell's
your problem, Brian?

17:41.183 --> 17:42.638
My-my problem?

17:42.706 --> 17:44.358
My-- right now my
problem seems to be

17:44.426 --> 17:45.997
that I am talking
to a Pelosi-lover.

17:46.065 --> 17:47.234
What?!
Yeah, that's right.

17:47.301 --> 17:48.537
You love Pelosi.

17:48.605 --> 17:50.476
You know what?
It's time for you to go.

17:50.544 --> 17:52.014
Right now.
Hey, fine.

17:52.065 --> 17:54.655
I don't have to sit here and
waste my time with a softie.

17:54.706 --> 17:55.908
You-you call
yourself a Republican?

17:55.976 --> 17:57.730
Republicans don't shy
away from a fight.

17:57.798 --> 17:59.201
And I'm gonna
prove it to you.

18:10.751 --> 18:12.138
Aha!

18:12.206 --> 18:13.608
Who are you?

18:13.676 --> 18:14.978
How did you get in here?

18:15.047 --> 18:16.267
Shut up, Pelosi.

18:16.334 --> 18:18.104
Are you here to take my baby?

18:18.172 --> 18:20.043
No, I'm here to strap
you to a board,

18:20.111 --> 18:22.433
put a cloth in your mouth
and pour water over it

18:22.502 --> 18:23.736
to simulate the
sensation of drowning.

18:23.805 --> 18:25.092
Yeah! Traditional values!

18:34.702 --> 18:36.791
Griffin, you been bailed out.

18:39.215 --> 18:41.320
Oh, Rush, thank God.

18:41.388 --> 18:42.690
Boy, you got down
hereuick.

18:42.758 --> 18:45.331
Yeah, I keep Strom Thurmond's
corpse in the front seat

18:45.399 --> 18:47.504
so I can use
the carpool lane.
Oh.

18:47.572 --> 18:49.008
Okay, well, come
on, let's go home.

18:49.076 --> 18:50.179
t idea.

18:50.247 --> 18:51.666
Tiou to go home.

18:51.734 --> 18:52.970
Home to the Griffins.

18:53.038 --> 18:54.874
Wh... What do you mean?

18:54.942 --> 18:56.680
That's where you
belong, Brian.

18:56.748 --> 18:58.118
You're not really
a conservative.

18:58.186 --> 18:59.321
What are you--
That's not true.

18:59.389 --> 19:00.424
I am conservative.

19:00.492 --> 19:01.662
I support the death penalty

19:01.729 --> 19:03.032
to show people
that killing is wrong.

19:03.099 --> 19:04.603
And that's great, Brian.

19:04.671 --> 19:06.608
Look, I-I make a living
persuading others

19:06.677 --> 19:08.012
to join my side.

19:08.080 --> 19:09.750
But I'd never,
ever want somebody

19:09.818 --> 19:11.222
to be something they're not.

19:11.290 --> 19:12.525
You're a liberal, Brian.

19:12.593 --> 19:14.297
I mean, what about
that four-year-old

19:14.365 --> 19:15.884
that was executed in Texas?

19:15.952 --> 19:18.325
There was a four-year-old
executed in Texas?

19:18.393 --> 19:21.935
Not really, but you see, Brian,
your concern betrays you.

19:22.002 --> 19:23.407
I know your type.

19:23.474 --> 19:25.110
It's not a coincidence
you turned your back

19:25.178 --> 19:27.150
on your democratic principles
just when the Democrats

19:27.217 --> 19:28.420
became the political
establishment.

19:28.487 --> 19:30.224
All you want is something
to fight against.

19:30.292 --> 19:32.264
I mean...

19:32.332 --> 19:34.353
I suppose we shouldn't
be executing children.

19:34.421 --> 19:35.356
You see?

19:35.425 --> 19:36.960
You're not really one of us.

19:37.028 --> 19:38.666
Oh, my God...

19:38.734 --> 19:40.671
Lois was right.

19:40.738 --> 19:44.516
Right there. See, the fact
that you would give a woman
credit for anything...

19:44.584 --> 19:46.287
it means you're
a liberal, Brian.

19:46.355 --> 19:50.265
It's time for you to spread
your two left wings and fly.

19:50.333 --> 19:53.507
Does this-- does this mean
I'll never see you again?

19:53.575 --> 19:55.965
Oh, I'll be around.

19:56.033 --> 19:57.602
Wherever there's
a rich white guy

19:57.669 --> 20:00.411
in need of another tax break,
I'll be there.

20:00.478 --> 20:02.382
Wherever there's
a brain-dead woman

20:02.450 --> 20:04.188
in need
of expensive life support

20:04.256 --> 20:07.096
her husband doesn't want,
I'll be there.

20:07.164 --> 20:09.502
Wherever there's a country
that needs to be invaded

20:09.571 --> 20:13.146
for reasons that don't exactly
pan out, I'll be there, too.

20:13.214 --> 20:15.454
Oh, yes, I will be around.

20:26.501 --> 20:27.571
Hey, Limbaugh.

20:29.210 --> 20:31.113
I think you're a boneheaded,
fascist,

20:31.181 --> 20:32.986
corporate-shilling blowhard.

20:33.054 --> 20:34.991
Look, you little smartass,

20:35.059 --> 20:37.799
I think you are a godless,
socialist, pot-smoking,

20:37.868 --> 20:39.270
maggot-infested member

20:39.338 --> 20:40.640
of the blame-America-first
crowd,

20:40.708 --> 20:42.681
and I think you want
the terrorists to win.

20:53.478 --> 20:54.983
(takes a deep breath)

20:54.984 --> 21:55.984
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru